;
READING ARCHIVES

DIR P0: lists SIG/M libraries; DIR P1: lists CPMUG libraries.
LDIR lists the members of an LBR without extracting it.
Example: LDIR P0:SIGMV011

LT reads plain text and supported compressed text, including LBR members.
Example: LT P0:SIGMV011 ABSTRACT.011
Use the names shown by LDIR when selecting a member.

A library may contain programs, source, documentation and supporting data.
Archive availability does not imply caller execution approval.
Download files with YSEND for use on your own CP/M system.
Use HELP TRANSFER for transfer instructions.
